/// HealthCheck — protocol for objects that can be polled by a Monitor.
///
/// Implementors run a check against some target and report the outcome
/// as a `CheckResult`. Concrete implementations include `HttpHealthCheck`
/// (HTTP GET), `TcpPortCheck` (TCP connect), and `ProcessCheck` (BEAM
/// process liveness). See SPEC.md section 1.
Protocol define: HealthCheck
  /// Run the check and return a CheckResult describing the outcome.
  check -> CheckResult
  /// Human-readable name for this check (used in alerts and logs).
  name -> String
  /// String describing the thing being checked (URL, host:port, process name, ...).
  target -> String
